From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase&): initialise members in
 the init-list

What: copies values and stringIndexes in the member-initialiser list instead of default-constructing both vectors and assigning them in the body.
Why it might be faster: saves two default constructions and two assignments per copy; fields are copied constantly while building messages. This is the largest single step of the series that has a clear mechanism (about 4% at search time).

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 13, region 134 (FieldBase::FieldBase).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.9804 -> 0.9369 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_13.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_field_base.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_field_base.cpp b/src/fit_field_base.cpp
index 2f8212c..f4c33d8 100644
--- a/src/fit_field_base.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_field_base.cpp
@@ -25,9 +25,8 @@ FieldBase::FieldBase(void)
 }
 
 FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
+    : values(field.values), stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
 {
-    values = field.values;
-    stringIndexes = field.stringIndexes;
 }
 
 FieldBase::~FieldBase()
